    "q-164264": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164264",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the vertex of the elliptic paraboloid $z-5=3(x-2)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The general equation of an elliptic paraboloid oriented along the $z$-axis with vertex at a point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the vertex, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-5 & =3(x-2)^{2}+2(y+1)^{2} \\\\ z-5 & =\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1/3}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{1/2} \\\\ z-5 & =\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1/3}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic paraboloid that has its vertex at $(2,-1,5).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
