    "q-35557": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35557",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the saddle point of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z+1=\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The general equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is \n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the saddle point, we rewrite our equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+1 & =\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-(-1) & =\\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid with a saddle point at $(-3,0,-1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
