    "q-35703": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35703",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $4(x-1)^{2}+25(y+1)^{2}=100(z-2)$ and the plane \n$z=7$  onto the $xy$-plane is an ellipse. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the ellipse?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the paraboloid and the plane $z=7$, we substitute $z=7$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+25(y+1)^{2}=100(z-2) \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+25(y+1)^{2}=100(7-2) \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+25(y+1)^{2}=500 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{125}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{20} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(5\\sqrt{5})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with semi-axes of lengths $5\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
